### ============================================================================
### IaC Deployment Assistant — HITL Workflow on Azure Durable Functions
### ============================================================================
### Pipeline: input_router → drafter → reviewer (HITL pause) → publisher
###
### The reviewer executor validates the Terraform, summarizes it, and pauses
### for human approval. When it pauses, a notify executor emails the reviewer a
### direct approve/reject link (the respond URL below), so the manual status +
### respond steps here are only a fallback. On rejection, the drafter
### re-generates incorporating feedback. On approval, the publisher pushes to ADO
### and creates a PR.
###
### Prerequisites:
### 1. Start Azurite: azurite --silent --location .
### 2. Start Durable Task Scheduler emulator
### 3. Configure local.settings.json (copy from local.settings.json.template)
### 4. az login
### 5. Run: func start
###
### BREAKING CHANGE — workflow routes are now scoped by workflow name. The newer
### agent-framework package renames the single-workflow routes from
###   /api/workflow/run, /api/workflow/status/{id}, /api/workflow/respond/{id}/{req}
### to
###   /api/workflow/{name}/run, /api/workflow/{name}/status/{id},
###   /api/workflow/{name}/respond/{id}/{req}
### The workflow here is named "iac_deployment", so every call below uses
### /api/workflow/iac_deployment/... . Update any old /api/workflow/run callers.
### ============================================================================

@host = https://<your-function>.azurewebsites.net or http://localhost:7071

@x_functions_key = <YOUR_FUNCTION_KEY_HERE_FOR_FUNCTION_APP_ONLY>
### 1. Start a new IaC workflow.

POST {{host}}/api/workflow/iac_deployment/run
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}

{
  "service": "App Service",
  "region": "westeurope",
  "options": "Linux plan, Standard S1 tier, with Application Insights"
}

### Another example — Storage Account with CDN.

POST {{host}}/api/workflow/iac_deployment/run
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}

{
  "service": "Storage Account",
  "region": "francecentral",
  "options": "Blob containers for media and backups, plus a CDN endpoint"
}

### ============================================================================
### 2. Check Workflow Status (fallback — the reviewer is emailed the link)
### ============================================================================

@instanceId = 6980aa08e1c049b8b791817012122443

GET {{host}}/api/workflow/iac_deployment/status/{{instanceId}}
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}

### ============================================================================
### 3. Approve the Terraform Review
### ============================================================================
### Use the link from the email, or the requestId from the status response.

@requestId = 6ed64b29-1b6c-4236-a034-024959f4bcb5

POST {{host}}/api/workflow/iac_deployment/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}

{
  "approved": true,
  "feedback": "Looks good, deploy it."
}

### ============================================================================
### 4. Reject and Request Changes
### ============================================================================
### The reviewer will re-draft incorporating your feedback.

POST {{host}}/api/workflow/iac_deployment/respond/{{instanceId}}/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}

{
  "approved": false,
  "feedback": "Use Premium v3 plan instead of Standard S1, and add a custom domain."
}

### ============================================================================
### Health Check
### ============================================================================

GET {{host}}/api/health
x-functions-key:{{x_functions_key}}
